rem 1. Arrays and matrices
use sequences
use numbers

rem A range gives us the numbers 1 through 6.
A = 1 to 6
rem Arithmetic applies to every number: 10 20 30 40 50 60.
A * 10
rem Arrays can combine element by element: 2 4 6 8 10 12.
A + A

rem Reshape the same six numbers into two rows of three.
M = A reshape 2 3
M
rem A scalar also works with a whole matrix.
M + 100

rem Try changing 100 to 10, or reshaping A into 3 rows of 2.
